BT 1 0 0 1 0 134 Tm 13 TL /F1 9 Tf .078431 .168627 .290196 rg (The title \223Python-Based Vulnerability Scanner\224 means that Python is the programming language used to develop) Tj T* (VulnGuard. It does not mean that the application scans only Python files. VulnGuard has three distinct checking) Tj T* (functions:) Tj  T* /F2 9 Tf (1. Dependency scanning:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( reads supported package/version entries, commonly from requirements.txt, and checks) Tj T* (them against OSV.dev.) Tj  T* /F2 9 Tf (2. Python source-code scanning:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( inspects uploaded .py source files for selected risky coding patterns.) Tj  T* /F2 9 Tf (3. Text-file credential scanning:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( inspects uploaded .txt content for patterns that may resemble passwords, API keys,) Tj T* (tokens, or private-key entries.) Tj  T*  T* (The text-file module is a credential-pattern checker, not a general-purpose security analyzer for every kind of text) Tj T* (content.) Tj T* ET
