BT 1 0 0 1 0 109.6 Tm 13.2 TL /F1 9.2 Tf .141176 .203922 .278431 rg (1\) The user opens the VulnGuard dashboard in a browser.) Tj  T* (2\) The user selects a supported input, such as a requirements-style dependency file, a Python source file, or a text) Tj T* (file.) Tj  T* (3\) Flask receives the upload and passes the content to the appropriate scanning module.) Tj  T* (4\) The dependency scanner extracts supported package/version entries and queries OSV.dev for known advisories.) Tj  T* (5\) The source scanner checks Python source text for selected patterns such as eval\(\), exec\(\), hardcoded secrets,) Tj T* (shell=True, and SQL f-strings.) Tj  T* (6\) The text scanner checks for patterns that may resemble passwords, API keys, tokens, or private-key material.) Tj  T* (7\) The application organizes the findings and displays them on the results page for the user to review.) Tj T* ET
