BT 1 0 0 1 0 202 Tm 13.2 TL /F2 9.2 Tf .141176 .203922 .278431 rg (A. Dependency Vulnerability Scanner) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf  T* (The dependency scanner accepts supported package/version entries, typically in a requirements-style format such) Tj T* (as package==version. It sends the package information to OSV.dev and displays matching advisory records when) Tj T* (available. Results may include advisory identifiers, summaries, affected package details, and severity information) Tj T* (where provided by the source.) Tj  T*  T* /F2 9.2 Tf (B. Python Source-Code Scanner) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf  T* (The source scanner reads uploaded .py files as text. It checks selected patterns that may indicate unsafe coding) Tj T* (practices, including eval\(\), exec\(\), hardcoded passwords or secrets, shell=True, and SQL f-strings. A finding includes) Tj T* (contextual information such as the issue type, filename, line number, and severity label where implemented. The) Tj T* (scanner does not execute the uploaded Python file.) Tj  T*  T* /F2 9.2 Tf (C. Text-File Credential Scanner) Tj /F1 9.2 Tf  T* (The text scanner checks uploaded .txt content for patterns that may resemble credentials, such as password, API) Tj T* (key, secret, token, or private-key entries. A match is a warning for manual review. It does not prove that a credential) Tj T* (is genuine, active, or compromised.) Tj T* ET
